.. warning::

    Geometry files and simulation results both use ``.h5``. For a single
    run, ``model.in`` produces ``model.h5`` by default. If the geometry
    input is that same file, saving the simulation results overwrites it
    without confirmation. Importing the geometry does not protect the
    original file from later output writes.

    Use distinct paths for geometry and results: for example, name the
    geometry file ``model_geometry.h5``, choose a separate output directory,
    or set a different result basename with ``-o`` on the command line or
    ``outputfile`` in the Python API. The same precaution applies when
    choosing a geometry-export filename.
